# 66. ⭐ KEY EXAM POINT

> **Static analysis examines malware without executing it, while dynamic analysis executes the sample in a controlled environment and observes its behavior. Effective malware analysis combines static, dynamic, behavioral, and network analysis to identify capabilities, persistence mechanisms, and Indicators of Compromise (IOCs).**